Clearcote: retain native IME compositionend trust through the scoped event queue

Why: Chromium 150 creates compositionstart/update via EventTarget::DispatchEvent,
which marks browser-generated events trusted. Native compositionend is deferred
through DispatchScopedEvent instead; that path preserves the constructor default
(false), including ImeCommitText, finish-on-blur and cancellation. Mark trust at
the browser-owned creation site, without changing script-created DOM events or
Event.prototype. This changes the isTrusted value visible to websites only for
native IME compositionend. JS dispatchEvent must continue to expose false.

Pinned source: Chromium 150.0.7871.114 (UPSTREAM_REVISION).
Regression: InputMethodControllerTest.NativeCompositionEndIsTrusted covers input
and contenteditable, each with commit, finish and cancellation. Cross-building
chrome does not execute this C++ test; the Windows artifact has a separate CDP
runtime probe, including the script-dispatch negative control.

--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/editing/ime/input_method_controller.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/editing/ime/input_method_controller.cc
@@ -406,6 +406,9 @@
 
   auto* event = MakeGarbageCollected<CompositionEvent>(
       event_type_names::kCompositionend, frame.DomWindow(), text);
+  // This browser-generated IME event bypasses EventTarget::DispatchEvent when
+  // queued. Preserve the trust assigned to compositionstart/compositionupdate.
+  event->SetTrusted(true);
   EventDispatcher::DispatchScopedEvent(*target, *event);
 }
 
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/editing/ime/input_method_controller_test.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/editing/ime/input_method_controller_test.cc
@@ -186,6 +186,38 @@
